  "behavior": [
    "Undo and Redo restore complete accepted immutable model snapshots across up to20 committed visit edits.",
    "Outcome selection is one step; accepted text in a single focused date/note field groups until blur or explicit action. Exact no-op keeps Redo; a real new edit clears it.",
    "Invalid drafts remain visible and block history, JSON, CSV and Print until corrected. Invalid text is never admitted as a successful edit.",
    "Recovery preserves sibling occurrences, source text, outcome/date/note values and literal CR/CRLF in the model. Null and empty distinctions are a model/JSON guarantee; the inherited CSV maps a null date to an empty field.",
    "Use starts a new history even for an equal record; canceled, failed and unconfirmed opens preserve history. Recovery retires pending file generations.",
    "JSON, CSV and Print use current restored data through unchanged retained handlers. Recovery restores field focus and scroll; native accessible buttons add no custom keyboard interception.",
    "History is page-session state, cleared on pagehide; no schema/provider/dependency/persistence change."
  ],
